# HOW IT IS SERVED
#   Vite copies public/ verbatim into dist/, and the nginx SPA catch-all
#   (`location / { try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html; }` in
#   /etc/nginx/sites-available/3speak.tv) serves any real file it finds before
#   falling through to index.html. That is exactly how /robots.txt already works,
#   so no nginx change is needed: the reason https://3speak.tv/ads.txt currently
#   answers 200 with text/html is simply that the file does not exist yet.
#
#   Verify after deploying:
#     curl -sI https://3speak.tv/ads.txt | grep -i content-type   # want text/plain
